Google Calendar rules:
- Do not create duplicate DailyFlow calendars.
- Before creating a DailyFlow calendar, always check whether one already exists and reuse it.
- DailyFlow-created events should be created only inside the dedicated DailyFlow Google Calendar.
- BusyBlocks and DailyFlow-created events are different concepts and must remain logically separated.
- BusyBlocks should represent occupied time from the user-selected Google calendars.
- Reuse existing Google OAuth/token refresh logic where possible.
- Current Google scopes should preserve both:
  - https://www.googleapis.com/auth/calendar.readonly
  - https://www.googleapis.com/auth/calendar.app.created
- If Google reconnect is triggered from a specific screen, the user should return to the same source screen after OAuth when possible.
- If implementing a return_to parameter for OAuth, only allow safe internal frontend paths and default to /calendar when missing or invalid.
- Do not create an open redirect risk.
- Do not create duplicate Google events when an item is already linked to an existing DailyFlow event.

Calendar / scheduling UI rules:
- App-owned displayed times should use 24-hour HH:mm format.
- Do not show AM/PM in DailyFlow UI.
- Add-to-calendar popups in Meals and Workouts should use controlled 24-hour HH:mm input if native browser time input displays AM/PM.
- In scheduling flows, selectable days should not include past days.
- Day labels should always be in English and should use this format:
  - Sunday 10.05
  - Monday 11.05
- Do not change actual ISO datetime values sent to Google Calendar unless needed to derive them correctly from the selected date/time.

Profile/settings rules:
- Screens should use the shared profile/preferences source.
- Do not create duplicate local preference state if existing profile data can be reused.
- Preferences changed in one screen should be reflected in other screens after save/navigation.
- Avoid adding new onboarding questionnaire questions unless explicitly requested.
- Keep real error messages for failed save/load/validation.
- Remove unnecessary helper notes or cluttered microcopy from the Profile/Preferences popup when requested.
- Profile and Preferences popup/modal should have consistent width and stable size between sections.
- Do not reintroduce Meal Preferences.

Workouts rules:
- Workouts implementation should remain stable and not be rewritten unless explicitly requested.
- Workout generation should use saved preferences and available free time.
- Existing saved/approved workout plan items should not disappear after Generate.
- Items added to Google Calendar should remain marked as added.
- Add to calendar must not create duplicate Google events.
- Delete should remove the linked DailyFlow-created event when applicable.
- Workout UI should stay consistent with Meals where appropriate, including subtle icons and pastel tag/category styling.
- If adding icons, use clean UI icons or inline SVGs, not emoji.
- Overview may READ Workout data and maintain its own completion state, but Overview completion must not modify the Workouts screen or Workouts plan state.

Meals & Grocery rules:
- Meals & Grocery implementation should remain stable unless explicitly requested.
- Meal Library, Saved Meals This Week, Grocery List, favorites, filters, servings, calendar flow, grocery generation, and PDF export already exist.
- Do not reintroduce Meal Preferences.
- Overview may read Meals calendar/scheduling data but should not duplicate or modify Meals functionality unless explicitly required.

Stress & Breaks current implementation:
Stress & Breaks is now an implemented product area.

It includes:
- Mandatory first-entry Stress & Breaks questionnaire.
- Questionnaire completion is separate from the global onboarding questionnaire.
- Edit Preferences.
- Activity Library with Timed / Flexible tabs.
- Favorites with a favorites-only filter.
- Generate Activities based on saved Stress preferences.
- Approximately 2–3 generated activities per relevant Timed category.
- Backend hard-capping prevents one category from flooding the generated library.
- Flexible activities come from a fixed catalog where appropriate.
- Weekly Break Plan.
- Timed activities are added with day + start time.
- Flexible activities are added with day + start time + selected duration.
- Weekly plan persists for the current week.
- Current-week plan follows Sunday–Saturday week boundaries.
- Old-week items must not appear in the current week.
- BusyBlocks conflict validation mirrors Workouts.
- BusyBlocks times may arrive as HH:MM:SS and must be parsed compatibly with Workouts.
- Half-open overlap semantics are used:
  max(start, block_start) < min(end, block_end)
- Add-to-calendar for individual Break activities.
- Add all to calendar.
- Google connect/reconnect behavior mirrors Workouts.
- Potentially Stressful Periods based on BusyBlocks + saved preferences.
- Potentially Stressful Periods provides guidance only and must never claim to detect actual stress.
- Potentially Stressful Periods is collapsible.
- Refresh Insights recalculates insights from current-week BusyBlocks/preferences and does not regenerate the Activity Library.
- Potentially Stressful Periods should remain compact and chronological.
- Generate Activities uses the same loading-overlay visual pattern as Workouts/Meals.

Stress YouTube rules:
- Curated YouTube support exists only for appropriate Timed categories:
  - Breathing
  - Meditation
  - Music / calming audio
- Stretching and Walking do not need YouTube videos for now.
- YouTube URLs must come only from a backend-owned curated catalog.
- OpenAI must never generate, guess, or override a YouTube URL or youtube_video_id.
- Curated catalog metadata includes stable IDs, category, URL, title, and exact duration.
- Video duration used by DailyFlow is:
  ceil(duration_seconds / 60)
- Example:
  - 7:24 video → 8 minutes
- Rounded video duration must propagate through:
  - Activity Library
  - Weekly Break Plan
  - BusyBlocks conflict validation
  - Google Calendar duration
- Relevant YouTube categories should contribute approximately 2–3 activities PER category on Generate.
- Do not expose the full curated pool at once.
- Recent curated video IDs are rotated per category so repeated Generate runs prefer different videos.
- Recent YouTube rotation state is stored in the existing StressBreaksLibrary item.
- Do not create a new table only for YouTube rotation.
- Watch Video should appear only for Timed activities with a valid curated video.
- Existing verified catalog entries must not be silently replaced with invented URLs.

