==================================================
OVERVIEW SCREEN SPECIFICATION
==================================================

Overview purpose:
The Overview screen gives the user a clear, attractive summary of the CURRENT WEEK across:
- Workouts
- Meals
- Stress & Breaks

It should summarize existing DailyFlow data rather than duplicate the full functionality of those screens.

The design should feel colorful, lively, modern, and visually engaging while remaining consistent with DailyFlow’s pastel design language.

Overview must use only TWO tabs:
- Summary
- Insights

Do NOT add a Patterns tab.

--------------------------------------------------
OVERVIEW WEEK RULES
--------------------------------------------------

Overview always represents the CURRENT WEEK only.

Week boundaries:
- Sunday through Saturday.

There is currently:
- no previous-week navigation
- no next-week navigation
- no week picker
- no historical Overview mode

On every:
- Overview screen entry
- browser refresh
- relevant data refresh

the Overview should derive the current Sunday–Saturday date range and fetch/read current data.

When a new Sunday starts, Overview naturally represents the new week.

Overview must not accidentally carry previous-week summary data into the new week.

All metrics and lists must be scoped to the current week.

--------------------------------------------------
OVERVIEW SUMMARY TAB
--------------------------------------------------

Summary contains three main colorful cards:

1. Workouts
2. Meals
3. Stress & Breaks

All three cards should be visually distinct but consistent.

Cards should be clickable and navigate to their corresponding screen:
- Workouts → Workouts screen
- Meals → Meals & Grocery screen
- Stress & Breaks → Stress & Breaks screen

Do not recreate the underlying screen inside Overview.

### Workouts card

The Workouts card should show:

- the user's weekly workout goal
- how many workouts were actually added to Google Calendar during the current week

Example:
2 / 3 scheduled

IMPORTANT:
“Scheduled” / “added” in Overview means added to the DailyFlow Google Calendar, not merely present in the Workouts Weekly Plan.

The Workouts card should also contain the workout list required for completion tracking.

For every current-week workout that has been added to Google Calendar, show:
- workout name
- day
- time
- Completed checkbox

Completed behavior:
- Completed exists ONLY in Overview.
- Do not add Completed UI/state to WorkoutsScreen.
- Checking Completed must not modify the Google Calendar event.
- Checking Completed must not remove or alter the Workout plan item.
- Completion state must persist across browser refresh and navigation.
- Completion state must be scoped to the relevant current-week workout.
- When the next week begins, previous-week completion state must not appear as current-week completion state.

Use stable IDs rather than workout title alone for completion persistence.

### Meals card

The Meals card should show:
- how many Meals were actually added to Google Calendar during the current week

Do not show a meal completion checklist.

Do not count Meal Library items that were not added to Google Calendar.

Card is clickable to Meals & Grocery.

### Stress & Breaks card

The Stress & Breaks card should show:
- how many Break activities were actually added to Google Calendar during the current week
- which current-week days were identified as potentially busy/stressful by the existing Stress insights logic

Example:
3 breaks scheduled
Busy days: Monday, Wednesday

Do not create a Break completion checklist.

Card is clickable to Stress & Breaks.

--------------------------------------------------
OVERVIEW INSIGHTS TAB
--------------------------------------------------

The Insights tab contains TWO concepts:

1. AI Weekly Insights
2. Daily Motivation

### AI Weekly Insights

Use OpenAI for the weekly insights.

Every explicit Insights refresh should generate fresh insight wording.

Generate:
- minimum 3 insights
- maximum 7 insights

Insights should be concise, useful, and grounded ONLY in real current-week DailyFlow data.

Relevant data may include:
- current-week workouts added to Google Calendar
- workout weekly goal
- Overview workout completion state
- current-week meals added to Google Calendar
- current-week Stress & Breaks activities added to Google Calendar
- current-week BusyBlocks
- current potentially busy/stressful days
- remaining days/time in the current week

OpenAI must not invent:
- workouts
- meals
- breaks
- BusyBlocks
- completed items
- dates
- calendar events
- free windows

Provide structured current-week data to OpenAI and validate/normalize the response before returning it to the frontend.

Insights should contain a mix of:
- observations
- progress feedback
- useful suggestions

Avoid repetitive wording.

### Actionable future suggestions

When appropriate, an insight may suggest a future opportunity.

Example:
The user's weekly workout goal is 3.
Only 2 workouts are scheduled.
The system may suggest a suitable open time for one more workout.

Such suggestions must follow these rules:

- Never suggest a day/time in the past.
- Search only from NOW through Saturday of the current week.
- Respect actual BusyBlocks/free-time information.
- Do not automatically schedule anything.
- Do not modify the Workout plan.
- The suggestion is guidance only.

If no appropriate future window exists, do not fabricate one.

### Insights refresh behavior

Refresh Insights should:
- read the latest current-week data
- call OpenAI again
- generate fresh insight wording
- return 3–7 insights
- update only the Overview Insights content

A refresh may produce different wording even if the underlying week data has not changed.

Use a loading state consistent with existing DailyFlow loading patterns.

--------------------------------------------------
DAILY MOTIVATION
--------------------------------------------------

The Insights tab should also include one visually prominent Daily Motivation card.

Daily Motivation does NOT need OpenAI.

Use a curated fixed pool of short motivational sentences appropriate for DailyFlow.

Show exactly ONE motivation sentence at a time.

The motivation sentence should rotate once per calendar day.

It should NOT change every time the user clicks Refresh Insights.

Prefer deterministic daily rotation based on the date so no additional database write is required solely for motivation.

The motivation card should:
- feel colorful
- stand out visually
- remain tasteful and consistent with the pastel DailyFlow style
- use no emoji unless explicitly requested

